  The reel_script says the monthly pension of Rs.6750 is for satthunavu and anganwadi employees, but the article says the Rs.6750 monthly pension is a demand separate from those employees' regular pay demand; the attribution is mixed up.
  The reel_script and slides_spec say the Rs.6750 monthly pension is for satthunavu (nutrition) employees, which the article does not state; the article links Rs.6750 to the pension demand generally.
  The caption merges the demands for satthunavu/anganwadi regular pay and the Rs.6750 pension into one sentence, mixing two different facts.
  The reel_script says the old pension demand was to 'reinstate' the scheme; the article says the new scheme should be cancelled and the old scheme provided, and it does not mention the TVK election promise. This is a minor missing nuance.
  The slides_spec line 'சத்துணவு ஊழியர்களுக்கு ரூ.6750 மாதாந்திர ஓய்வூதியம் கோரிக்கை' attributes the Rs.6750 pension to satthunavu employees, which contradicts the article.
  The reel_script omits the article's key point that the demand includes the TAPS scheme cancellation linked to the TVK (த.வெ.க.) election promise, which is an important stated cause of the protest.
